\section{Check Occupancy and Data, Including a Stall}

\begin{verbatim}
reference = empty
at each sampled edge with reset inactive:
    old = reference                 # pre-edge head
    check out_valid == old.present
    if out_valid: check out_data == old.word
    pop  = out_valid and out_ready
    push = in_valid and in_ready
    if pop: reference = empty       # check the OLD payload
    if push:
        assert reference == empty   # never overwrite an unread word
        reference = some(in_data)
# On reset: check neither handshake is advertised, then clear.
\end{verbatim}

After reset, send \(A\) while the consumer is stalled. Hold it stalled for another edge: \texttt{out\_valid} and \(A\) must persist, without another push. Then have the consumer accept \(A\) while the producer offers \(B\), so the next observable word is \(B\) with no validity gap. Also assert the readiness equation independently: the reference's data-order checks alone would not notice a device refusing all legal input. An unknown control is a simulation error to diagnose with the testbench, not a fifth case in the binary protocol.
